==== Opening the case ====

It's the same procedure as for TP-Link WR741ND ([[tl-wr741nd#opening_the_case|see here for instructions]])

==== Serial ====
To access the serial console of the wr743nd, you need
  - Solder a bridge like the two red points
  - Connect a usb serial device (dku-5, ca-42) to Tx, Rx, Gnd.

Bits per second: **115200**\\
Data bits: **8**\\
Parity: **None**\\
Stop bits: **1**\\
Flow control: **None**\\

{{media:tplink:tl-wr743:tl-wr743nd_serial.jpg?300}}

The above setup may not work (rendering serial console readonly). In that case, try soldering different bridge:

{{media:tplink:tl-wr741:tl-wr741nd-v1.1_serial.jpg?300}}

